      "sourceHash": "276b39e2deb478ea28999e958a70f8fd25e094cd77848dab6681ec62827162a4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.7,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "-: Now with our pipes being added and parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 6.87,
          "en": "it's all important to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.87,
          "end": 9.75,
          "en": "that you can combine pipes in angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.75,
          "end": 12.36,
          "en": "So far we only use pipes on their own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.36,
          "end": 14.01,
          "en": "So we added the date pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.01,
          "end": 17.07,
          "en": "to our servers, started output here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.07,
          "end": 20.19,
          "en": "and we added the Apple case pipe to the instance type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.19,
          "end": 24.111,
          "en": "Now what if we wanted to, yes, form date like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.111,
          "end": 29.111,
          "en": "but then for some reason also make it all uppercase?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.28,
          "end": 31.642,
          "en": "Now you can simply chain pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.642,
          "end": 34.053,
          "en": "by adding a pipe symbol after a pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.053,
          "end": 37.26,
          "en": "So it could add uppercase here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.26,
          "end": 40.26,
          "en": "Now the order might be important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.26,
          "end": 43.586,
          "en": "Generally it will be parsed from left to right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.586,
          "end": 48.586,
          "en": "So service started gets into this pipe here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.132,
          "end": 49.98,
          "en": "So the date pipe gets applied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.98,
          "end": 52.5,
          "en": "to our service started property output here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.5,
          "end": 54.69,
          "en": "to the string population.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.69,
          "end": 57.63,
          "en": "The uppercase pipe then gets applied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 60.03,
          "en": "to the result of this operation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.03,
          "end": 63.298,
          "en": "And I can show this if I save it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.298,
          "end": 66.799,
          "en": "You see that the date indeed is upper case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.799,
          "end": 70.08,
          "en": "Now, if I switch positions here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.08,
          "end": 75.08,
          "en": "and put the upper case pipe first and then parse the date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.968,
          "end": 79.41,
          "en": "you see we get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.41,
          "end": 83.14,
          "en": "And if we open up the console and view this error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84,
          "end": 87.9,
          "en": "you see that this argument here is not correct",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.9,
          "end": 89.01,
          "en": "for the upper case pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.01,
          "end": 90.63,
          "en": "It doesn't know how to parse it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.63,
          "end": 93.15,
          "en": "because it is a date and not a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.15,
          "end": 95.31,
          "en": "and there are elements which can't be turned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.31,
          "end": 97.08,
          "en": "into upper case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.08,
          "end": 102.08,
          "en": "So this is why it's important to watch the order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.36,
          "end": 103.89,
          "en": "You should apply the pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.89,
          "end": 107.34,
          "en": "in the order you want to transform your input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.34,
          "end": 108.81,
          "en": "So transforming the date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.81,
          "end": 112.2,
          "en": "into something which can be parsed first is absolutely fine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.2,
          "end": 115.59,
          "en": "and as you will see, will work correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.59,
          "end": 116.675,
          "en": "You see it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.675,
          "end": 120.06,
          "en": "but the other way around wouldn't work in this example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.06,
          "end": 124.56,
          "en": "So again, always keep this order in mind from left to right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.56,
          "end": 128.047,
          "en": "this is how it gets executed and how pipes get applied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.047,
          "end": 131.482,
          "en": "With that out of the way, let's create our own pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.482,
          "end": 134.76,
          "en": "in case there is some functionality we need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.76,
          "end": 138.03300000000002,
